<spell-notebook "breadcrumb theming">
	<header level="1">
		Breadcrumb
		<header>A breadcrumb is used to show hierarchy between content.</>
	</>
	<breadcrumb-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
				<ui-item link="#themes">Themes</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-breadcrumb-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (a header, `:root`), or
			on the breadcrumb's box through `::part(breadcrumb)`. The sections inherit them from the breadcrumb, so set them
			there or above, not on a section.

			The text divider is the `--ui-breadcrumb-divider` token (a CSS string), so a whole site can change it once
			instead of setting `divider` on every breadcrumb; a `divider` attribute still wins.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			header ui-breadcrumbs {
			  --ui-breadcrumb-divider: "»";
			  --ui-breadcrumb-divider-color: var(--ui-primary);
			  --ui-breadcrumb-active-font-weight: normal;
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				`size` scales every token measured in `em`; `inverted` switches the breadcrumb to the dark scheme, so its colour
				tokens resolve to their dark values. Never set the `--_ui-*` names: they're the sheet's private plumbing.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-breadcrumbs" playground>
				<ui-breadcrumbs aria-label="Breadcrumb demo">
					<ui-breadcrumb link="#home">Home</>
					<ui-breadcrumb link="#store">Store</>
					<ui-breadcrumb selected>T-Shirt</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
